<title>AUSTRALIA: Defiance disappointed at NZ sale rejection.</title>
<headline>Defiance disappointed at NZ sale rejection.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-04-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Defiance Mills Ltd said on Monday it was disappointed by the New Zealand Commerce Commission's rejection of the NZ$48 million sale of its NZ milling and baking assets to Goodman Fielder Ltd.</p>
<p>Defiance chairman Tom O'Brien said the conditional sale agreement would remain alive while both parties reviewed the implication of the decision.</p>
<p>&quot;We will study the findings of the Commerce Commission to determine how we can facilitate the transaction so that it is acceptable to all parties,&quot; O'Brien said in a statement.</p>
</text>
